Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:51:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] OW-028 (lane-279): ROCmFP4-FAST q8_1 MMVQ route DEFAULT ON
 for FP4-format files

President YES 2026-09-24 (HQ seat 64): FP4 MMVQ default-ON ships for FP4-file users; zero change to our serving (the seated Q4_K_XL line carries no q4_0_rocmfp4_fast tensors); synonym divergence documented. A ruling, not new evidence; the F-13 probes stay open, non-blocking.

- ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq_impl: the admit keys on GGML_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST only (n=3,5 width gate unchanged); device->rocmfp4_mmvq_route probed once, default ON, GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=0 opts out, =1 (lane-206 opt-in value) still ON.
- Startup line: "fp4 mmvq route: route (q4_0_rocmfp4_fast, n=3,5) (default, FP4 formats)" / "legacy (f32 dequant) (GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=0)".
- docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md FP4 row + protected-wins.json: default and divergence note (R86d stage 3, 2/6 prompts, opt-out named).

Gates (all executed): build rc=0; MUL_MAT 2305/2305 + MUL_MAT_ID 1004/1004, 0 FAIL, default and legacy arms; trace census MMVQ at n=3,5 only (default), 0 MMVQ rows (legacy); RED sign-flip in the FP4 mmvq_dot_a: default 32/99 FAIL all at n=3/5, legacy 99/99, restore sha d684ee74 + regreen 99/99; greedy identity DEFAULT vs LEGACY differ 2/6 (prompts 4,5 at chars 238/252), control 6/6, each arm byte-identical to its R86d counterpart 6/6.

