x cells** — prefill and decode reported separately at three prompt lengths, every arm range overlapping. Identity: **byte-identical output, one distinct sha256 per prompt across 6 serve launches (18 completions)**. Correctness `test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT` **1394/1394, 0 FAIL, both arms**.<br>**Kept on the distributable-engine ground, not on a measured gain:** strictly less work — one fewer workgroup barrier per row per superblock and no shared tile — for a bit-identical result.<br>**What it did NOT fix, stated:** `q6_K` mat-vec runs **~35% below `q5_K`** at the identical shape (`m=17408 n=3 k=5120`: **41.0 vs 63.8 GB/s**, ratio 0.643), every `q6_K` row in a 39.2–41.6 band. The per-row barrier was the leading mechanism for that deficit and is now **FALSIFIED**; the deficit is **OPEN**. Correction to the motivating claim: `q4_K` at that same shape is **60.6 GB/s, not 72.5** — the deficit survives on the `q5_K` comparison only. See [`FINDINGS.md`](FINDINGS.md) F-14. |
