1 is a measured tie; width 4 is a tie; width 2 is the width that changed a sampled token; above 5 the port loses. | **MEASURED WIN, DEFAULT ON BY PRESIDENT RULING 2026-09-24 (OW-028).** The default changed because of the ruling, not because of new evidence. The F-13 items named at the end of this cell are still OPEN and do not block the default. Ladder, RIG-A, `m=17408 k=5120`, 3-round medians, epoch E2: `n=1` ×0.991, `n=2` ×1.192, **`n=3` ×1.361**, `n=4` ×1.018, **`n=5` ×1.310**, `n=8` ×1.025. Epoch E1 read ×0.998 / ×1.183 / ×1.335 / ×1.015 / ×1.316 / ×1.040 — **the gains reproduce across a driver change**. The discriminator is the control arm: under `GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1` both arms take the identical f32 shader and every row flattens to **×0.991–1.007**, so this is the port and not build drift. Ungated at `n=8` the port read **×0.796**, which is why the gate has an upper bound at all.<br>**Serve, epoch E2** (julianmb Qwen3.8-27B-ROCmFP4-FAST 14.56 GB, DFlash2 depth 2, palindrome, 16 rounds/slot): drafted decode **7.498 → 9.518 t/s mean, +2.0199 [1.3212, 2.7186], 8/8 cells positive = +27%**; median 7.461 → 9.282. Plain **5.084 → 5.086, +0.0016 [−0.0168, +0.0199] = tied**. Prefill tied. Rolled **32/40 → 33/40**. **Zero empty completions in 64 rounds.** F-141 **0/8** on all three slots; `test-backend-ops` **10 MUL_MAT + 2 MUL_MAT_ID cases, 0 FAIL**.<br>**BLOCKING RESIDUAL, and it is why widths 2 and 4 are excluded:** an earlier build of this port made the model emit an empty completion — first token end-of-generation — deterministically on one prompt on this file. Three hypotheses were falsified before the cause was isolated to **width 2** (the n=1 dispatch gate did not remove it; a slot-swap proved the empties follow the **binary**, not the slot; forcing f32 for the whole run removed them). The same shader arithmetic is **still live at widths 3 and 5**, and the reproducer is a plain sequence that cannot reach them. Still OPEN (was "owed before default-branch integration"; now non-blocking after the 2026-09-24 ruling): an adversarial drafted-mode cache-history corpus reaching width 3, or an MMVQ-vs-f32 logits comparison, or a tightened backend error gate. See [`FINDINGS.md`](FINDINGS.md) F-13. |
 | `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` | **THIS ROW INVERTED on 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b phase 2) - read it before assuming the old default.** **ON when unset, wherever the MMVQ A-side hoist is live** (device-probed ON for AMD): `GGML_TYPE_SX8` takes the `q8_1` integer-dot mat-vec at EVERY width, and only an exact `0` hands it back to the whole-block f32 route. Where the hoist is off (`GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0`, non-AMD) or the routing is pinned back (`GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy`), the pre-R48b rule below still holds: **OFF when unset, only an exact `1` admits the type**. The character test is unchanged in both directions (`env[0]`, not `atoi()` - they disagree on `"2"` and `"01"`). | Scope: the `q8_1` integer-dot `mul_mat_vec` pipeline for `GGML_TYPE_SX8` and nothing else, on the plain `MUL_MAT` path. The `_id` path calls the same predicate and so now admits the type as well, but `ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec_id()` still returns `nullptr` for S-X8 at `b_type == Q8_1` and the caller's `if (dmmv == nullptr)` branch (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:13246-13250`) clears `quantize_y` and reselects the f16 dequant pipeline - CHECKED, not assumed: `MUL_MAT_ID -b Vulkan0` is a receipt of this commit. | **Default. Enable the `0` arm only to pair against the whole-block route, or on a device where the hoist is off.** | **The pre-R48b evidence for the OFF default, and what superseded it.** The n=7 cliff that kept this OFF was an A-side re-decode in the mat-vec nest, and lane-235/R48b removed it. Under forced MMVQ with the hoist ON, S-X8 is FLAT at the bus at `n=1..8` (248320x5120: `74.8/75.2/72.1/73.6/74.2/74.7/73.7/72.8` GB/s; FFN shapes 36-37 at every width) against `62/70/33.5/45.5` at `n=5..8` with the hoist OFF, and beats the SHIPPED whole-block route by **+40..+110% at n>=4** on 248320x5120 and **+15 / +34% at n=2/3** on 17408x5120 (`32-paired-r48bforce.txt` vs `32-paired-r46iq.txt`, HQ, 3 quiet interleaved rounds, same binary both arms). **Still owed: a DEFAULT-routing re-pair** - every 